{"questions":[{"question_id":"hnFTStN1HDiGYFR0","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2012 Paper 2 Offline","year":2012,"examDate":2012,"subject":"physics","chapter":"properties-of-matter","chapterGroup":"mechanics","topic":"pressure-density-pascals-law-and-archimedes-principle","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":0.75,"permalink":"a-thin-uniform-cylindrical-shell-closed-at-both-ends-is-pa-2012-marks-3-hnftstn1hdigyfr0.htm","content":"A thin uniform cylindrical shell, closed at both ends, is partially filled with water. It is floating\nvertically in water in half-submerged state. If <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.489ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.05ex\" height=\"1.489ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 906.2 658\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(550,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D450\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D450\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> is the relative density of the material of the shell\nwith respect to water, then the correct statement is that the shell is","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"more than half-filled if <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.489ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.05ex\" height=\"1.489ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 906.2 658\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(550,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D450\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D450\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> is less than 0.5.\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"more than half-filled if <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.489ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.05ex\" height=\"1.489ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 906.2 658\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(550,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D450\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D450\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> is more than 1.0."},{"identifier":"C","content":"half-filled if <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.489ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.05ex\" height=\"1.489ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 906.2 658\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(550,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D450\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D450\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> is more than 0.5."},{"identifier":"D","content":"less than half-filled if <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.489ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.05ex\" height=\"1.489ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 906.2 658\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(550,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D450\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D450\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> is less than 0.5."}],"correct_options":["A"],"explanation":"<p>Consider a thin, uniform cylindrical shell that is closed at both ends and partially filled with water. This cylindrical shell is floating vertically in water, with exactly half of its height submerged. The relative density of the shell's material compared to water is denoted by <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.489ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.05ex\" height=\"1.489ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 906.2 658\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(550,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D450\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D450\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>.</p>\n\n<p>The inner radius of the cylindrical shell is <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.008ex\" height=\"1.339ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 887.6 592\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(484,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, the outer radius is <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.008ex\" height=\"1.339ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 887.6 592\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(484,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, the height is <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.303ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 576 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"210E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-210E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, and the material density is <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.489ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.17ex\" height=\"1.489ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 517 658\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70C\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>. The shell is filled with water, which has a density of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.489ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.503ex\" height=\"1.489ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 1106.3 658\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(550,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D464\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D464\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, up to a height of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 572 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D465\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D465\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>. Given <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -1.126ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"7.833ex\" height=\"2.948ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -805.3 3462 1303\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(550,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D450\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D450\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1184,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\" transform=\"translate(2239.7,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(428.3,492.7) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D70C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(550,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D464\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D464\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"982.3\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, we know that the cylinder is in a half-submerged state, meaning <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.566ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.566ex\" height=\"2.262ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 1576 1000\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"210E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-210E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(576,0)\"><use data-c=\"2F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1076,0)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> of the cylinder's height is submerged in water.</p>\n\n<img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1lzw1mwuq/ed8e01bf-65e6-407a-b719-6d6f14868978/ab4f4b20-5b70-11ef-965d-abded2122fc9/file-jaoe38c1lzw1mwur.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1lzw1mwuq/ed8e01bf-65e6-407a-b719-6d6f14868978/ab4f4b20-5b70-11ef-965d-abded2122fc9/file-jaoe38c1lzw1mwur.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;max-height:40vh;vertical-align:baseline\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2012 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Properties of Matter Question 53 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1lzw1mwuq/ed8e01bf-65e6-407a-b719-6d6f14868978/ab4f4b20-5b70-11ef-965d-abded2122fc9/file-jaoe38c1lzw1mwur.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1lzw1mwuq/ed8e01bf-65e6-407a-b719-6d6f14868978/ab4f4b20-5b70-11ef-965d-abded2122fc9/file-jaoe38c1lzw1mwur.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1lzw1mwuq/ed8e01bf-65e6-407a-b719-6d6f14868978/ab4f4b20-5b70-11ef-965d-abded2122fc9/file-jaoe38c1lzw1mwur.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/jaoe38c1lzw1mwuq/ed8e01bf-65e6-407a-b719-6d6f14868978/ab4f4b20-5b70-11ef-965d-abded2122fc9/file-jaoe38c1lzw1mwur.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/jaoe38c1lzw1mwuq/ed8e01bf-65e6-407a-b719-6d6f14868978/ab4f4b20-5b70-11ef-965d-abded2122fc9/file-jaoe38c1lzw1mwur.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/jaoe38c1lzw1mwuq/ed8e01bf-65e6-407a-b719-6d6f14868978/ab4f4b20-5b70-11ef-965d-abded2122fc9/file-jaoe38c1lzw1mwur.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">\n\n<p>In equilibrium, the weight of the cylindrical shell, including the water inside it, must equal the buoyant force (upthrust) acting on it. This relationship can be expressed as follows:</p>\n\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.791ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"40.99ex\" height=\"2.792ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -884.7 18117.5 1234.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(0 -0.5)\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-SO-28\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(458,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msubsup\" transform=\"translate(1031,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(484,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(484,-287.9) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2140.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(3141,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msubsup\" transform=\"translate(3714,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(484,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(484,-287.9) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(4601.6,0) translate(0 -0.5)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-SO-29\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(5226.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"210E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-210E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"trans